Depth profiling changes the specimen it measures (@cm-surface-profile: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/XPS-Planning-Interpretation-and-Reporting-Baer.lingua#r_6CY69TZ791W5PW0SZCY536SVH5", #source "../sources/XPS-Attenuation-and-Information-Depth-Powell.lingua#r_0RF0DVE5MXB1BAG8S0W48X46TV", #clean-manufacturing "Complementary-methods-can-test-a-shared-surface-model.lingua#r_1GC9KZT5NSDZTVC1X0BMPMQFJR") { r_1A7T7VWASDBMTJY6Z9MK8XG9TN
**Read:** [Planning and interpreting XPS — Baer and colleagues](../sources/XPS-Planning-Interpretation-and-Reporting-Baer.lingua#r_6CY69TZ791W5PW0SZCY536SVH5), depth resolution and sputtering; [Attenuation and information depth in XPS — Cedric Powell](../sources/XPS-Attenuation-and-Information-Depth-Powell.lingua#r_0RF0DVE5MXB1BAG8S0W48X46TV), information depth.

A depth profile may infer position from material removed between observations. Sputter time becomes depth only through a removal-rate relation, which can depend on composition, structure and operating state. Preferential removal, mixing, roughening and chemical change can alter the observed profile.

Even without specimen alteration, finite depth sensitivity broadens a sharp interface. In a teaching model where a step is blurred by a normalized Gaussian of standard deviation σ, the 10–90% transition width is about 2.56310σ. For σ = 2 nm, an atomically sharp modeled step appears about 5.12621 nm wide. This is an observation-kernel example, not a universal instrument-resolution formula.

Combining independent Gaussian broadening contributions gives σ_total² = Σσ_i² in that specific model. Real asymmetric mixing and attenuation kernels need not follow this rule. A fitted broad interface can represent actual intermixing, observation blur or both.

**Work:** Derive the blurred step from a convolution and verify the width numerically. Compare two specimen profiles that become difficult to distinguish after measurement. Explain what an independent thickness reference, a changed observation geometry or another method could establish. Treat a depth-profile inversion as evidence under a model rather than a direct photograph of the original layers.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
